{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>For the leader, for the sons of Korah, upon Alamot</b> — the name of a musical composition. Some say: this poet was of the seed of the sons of Korah, in the days of Hezekiah, when Sennacherib turned back. And the correct view in my eyes: that it speaks concerning Jerusalem, concerning the wars."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 46, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:30:59.043536917Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}